;;; tests/memory/vm_region_growth_watchdog_test.esk — the SW-14 fixture, gated
;;; by vm_region_growth_watchdog_test.sh and by vm_region_flat_rss_test.sh.
;;;
;;; A per-iteration `(with-region ...)` around a body that allocates and then
;;; drops everything it allocated. This is the shape the memory model documents
;;; as the way to keep a resident loop flat
;;; (docs/reference/runtime/memory-model.md).
;;;
;;; WHAT IT MEASURED BEFORE. On the bytecode VM it was not flat, and nothing
;;; about the program said so: the answer was right, the exit status was 0, and
;;; RSS climbed until the host gave out. Measured at the branch point, this
;;; fixture peaked at the SAME RSS with the `with-region` wrapper as without it
;;; — 1.503 GB against 1.504 GB — because the form reclaimed nothing there.
;;;
;;; WHAT IT MEASURES NOW. The Stage-1 region evacuator
;;; (lib/backend/vm_region_evac.c) made the wrapper real: the same fixture holds
;;; flat peak RSS as its iteration count is swept, which is the SW-14 close
;;; condition. vm_region_flat_rss_test.sh sweeps it and compares against
;;; ESHKOL_VM_REGION_EVAC=0 on the same binary; vm_region_growth_watchdog_test.sh
;;; uses it to pin that the heap-growth watchdog no longer fires for a loop that
;;; gets its memory back, while still firing for the same volume unwrapped.
;;;
;;; 64000 iterations x 120 conses: enough arena to cross a 64 MB budget on
;;; every supported host when nothing reclaims, and the sum is a pure function
;;; of the loop bounds so the printed answer pins that neither the guard nor
;;; the evacuator changed any behaviour.
;;;
;;; This was 4000 iterations until the per-object footprint it was tuned
;;; against changed: HeapObject's closure branch held its captures inline
;;; (`Value upvalues[N]`), which sized the union — and so every cons cell,
;;; since HeapObject is a tagged union shared by every heap subtype — at
;;; several hundred bytes or more. Moving closure capture storage out to a
;;; separately-sized allocation (commit 91e279dd, lossless beyond commit
;;; eba46f59) is a deliberate memory-efficiency win: sizeof(HeapObject) is now
;;; 40 bytes, so 4000 x 120 conses (~19 MB of tracked arena) no longer crosses
;;; a 64 MB budget on any host, and the watchdog it exists to pin went quiet.
;;; 64000 iterations restores comfortable headroom (~290 MB) above the budget
;;; against the current, smaller footprint.
(define (scratch-step k)
  (with-region ('step 65536)
    (let loop ((i 0) (acc '()))
      (if (< i 120)
          (loop (+ i 1) (cons (* i k) acc))
          (length acc)))))

(define (drive n total)
  (if (= n 0)
      total
      (drive (- n 1) (+ total (scratch-step n)))))

;; 64000 iterations x 120 conses: enough arena to cross a 64 MB budget on every
;; supported host, and the sum is a pure function of the loop bounds so the
;; printed answer pins that the guard changed no behaviour.
(display (drive 64000 0))
(newline)
